  "question": {
    "text": "A layer of oil with density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>724</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mn>m</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> floats on water of density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mn>m</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>. A block floats on the oil-water interface with <math><mn>1/6</mn></math> of its volume in oil and <math><mn>5/6</mn></math> of its volume in water, as shown in the figure. What is the density of the block?<br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/fbtoivqbqbkidmskhllogvqsivemxyaaizhguzyjwigqhtcuhu.jpeg\" />",
